1
00:04:55,862 --> 00:05:01,862
Prepare to be blown out of the water.

2
00:09:51,724 --> 00:09:57,724
Pirates of the Caribbean: The Curse of the Black Pearl is a
adventure, fantasy, action film directed by Gore Verbinski.

3
00:14:47,586 --> 00:14:53,586
When wily Captain Barbossa steals Jack Sparrow's ship and kidnaps the governor's beautiful daughter, Elizabeth, her
childhood friend Will Turner joins forces with Jack to save her and recapture Jack's ship, the Black Pearl.

4
00:19:43,448 --> 00:19:49,448
Jack Sparrow, played by Johnny Depp.

5
00:24:39,310 --> 00:24:45,310
Barbossa, played by Geoffrey Rush.

6
00:29:35,172 --> 00:29:41,172
Will Turner, played by Orlando Bloom.

7
00:34:31,034 --> 00:34:37,034
Elizabeth Swann, played by Keira Knightley.

8
00:39:26,896 --> 00:39:32,896
Norrington, played by Jack Davenport.

9
00:44:22,758 --> 00:44:28,758
Governor Weatherby Swann, played by Jonathan Pryce.

10
00:49:18,620 --> 00:49:24,620
Pirates of the Caribbean: The Curse of the Black Pearl is a 2003
American fantasy swashbuckler film directed by Gore Verbinski.

11
00:54:14,482 --> 00:54:20,482
Produced by Jerry Bruckheimer and distributed by Buena Vista Pictures via the Walt Disney Pictures label, the film is based on the
Pirates of the Caribbean attraction at Disney theme parks and is the first film in the Pirates of the Caribbean series.

12
00:59:10,344 --> 00:59:16,344
Starring Johnny Depp, Geoffrey Rush, Orlando Bloom, and Keira Knightley, it follows pirate Jack Sparrow (Depp) and the
blacksmith Will Turner (Bloom), as they attempt to rescue the kidnapped Elizabeth Swann (Knightley).

13
01:04:06,206 --> 01:04:12,206
The trio encounters Captain Hector Barbossa (Rush) and the Black
Pearl crew who are afflicted by a supernatural curse.

14
01:09:02,068 --> 01:09:08,068
Executives at Walt Disney Studios drafted a rough
treatment for  the film in 2000.

15
01:13:57,931 --> 01:14:03,931
A script was developed by Jay Wolpert in 2001, and was
rewritten by Stuart Beattie in early 2002.

16
01:18:53,793 --> 01:18:59,793
Around that time, the producer Jerry Bruckheimer became involved in the project.

17
01:23:49,655 --> 01:23:55,655
He brought in screenwriters Ted Elliott and Terry Rossio, who
had drafted a premise for the film in the 1990s.

18
01:28:45,517 --> 01:28:51,517
Elliott and Rossio added the curse to the script to align
the film's story with the theme park ride.

19
01:33:41,379 --> 01:33:47,379
Verbinski eventually signed on as the director.

20
01:38:37,241 --> 01:38:43,241
Filming took place from October 2002 to March 2003 in Saint Vincent and
the Grenadines and on sets in Los Angeles, California.

21
01:43:33,103 --> 01:43:39,103
Pirates of the Caribbean had its world premiere at the Disneyland
Resort in Anaheim, California, on June 28, 2003.

22
01:48:28,965 --> 01:48:34,965
It was theatrically released in the United States on July 9.

23
01:53:24,827 --> 01:53:30,827
Despite low expectations, the film was a massive box-office success: it grossed $654.3
million worldwide, making it the fourth-highest-grossing film of 2003.

24
01:58:20,689 --> 01:58:26,689
It received generally positive reviews from critics, and
Depp won a Screen Actors Guild Award.

25
02:03:16,551 --> 02:03:22,551
He was also nominated for his performance at the
Academy Awards, BAFTAs, and Golden Globes.

26
02:08:12,413 --> 02:08:18,413
Pirates of the Caribbean was also nominated for
additional Academy Awards and BAFTAs.

27
02:13:08,275 --> 02:13:14,275
The film was followed by four sequels: Dead Man's Chest (2006), At World's End
(2007), On Stranger Tides (2011), and Dead Men Tell No Tales (2017).

28
02:18:04,137 --> 02:18:10,137
The film explores themes of blacksmith, gold, exotic island, governor, skeleton.
